      "question": {
        ":question/id": "2bbbf3e9-50a2-5633-afa7-54f01477c957",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=-3 \\\\ 3x+ky &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 3 & k & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 3 & k & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & k+9 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=-3 \\\\ (k+9)y &=9.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-9,$ then the second equation is $0=9,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-9.$",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "a8ef3ea6-ecf7-556c-89b2-760afc491e03",
