        ":question/problem": "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=-2 \\\\ -2x+ky &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & k & -8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & k & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & k-4 & -12\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=-2 \\\\ (k-4)y &=-12.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=4,$ then the second equation is $0=-12,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=4.$",
